About Us
Newground Water Services is a leading provider of Irrigation consultation, installation and maintenance services. We pride ourselves on delivering high-quality work and exceptional customer service. Our team is dedicated to innovation, safety, and sustainability, and we are committed to providing rewarding career opportunities for our employees.
About The Role
The Graduate Civil Engineer will be responsible for project delivery for a range of projects across commercial irrigation, sports turf construction, drainage and water infrastructure ensuring that they meet budgets, agreed timeframes, quality standards and client expectations.
- Oversee projects from start to finish, ensuring work is completed safely, on time, and within budget.
- Coordinate employees, subcontractors, suppliers, and equipment across multiple project sites.
- Maintain strong relationships with clients and provide regular project updates.
- Monitor project costs, schedules, and progress to ensure successful project delivery.
- Ensure all work meets quality standards and complies with WHS, environmental, and contractual requirements.
Qualifications and Background
- Tertiary qualification in relevant discipline such as Engineering or Project Management;
- Extensive experience in the delivery of projects in a construction environment;
- National Construction Induction Certificate (White Card);
- Relevant experience in a similar role;
- Intermediate experience in the efficient utilisation of information systems and technology; and
- C class Drivers Licence.
 Skills and Experience
- Intermediate computing, numeracy and literacy skills;
- Advanced organisational skills with the ability to prioritise competing tasks;
- Advanced customer service skills;
- Advanced communication and problem-solving skills;
- Intermediate negotiation and influencing skills;
- Knowledge of project management principles and practices;
- Knowledge of building construction practices and methodology; and
- Knowledge of the practical application of Work Health and Safety measures in the workplace.
We will be reviewing applications now so apply today!

About Us
ADW Johnson is a multi-disciplinary company specialising in Urban Design, Planning, Engineering, Project Management, Surveying and Landscape Architecture with offices in Newcastle, the Central Coast, and in Sydney. We are passionate about development and treat each and every project as if it is our own. We use our expertise, dedication and hard work to forge long-term relationships with our clients and deliver best development outcomes. 
About The Opportunity
We are now looking for a Trainee Draftsperson to join our company at our Central Coast office.
With the wide variety of land development, high end residential and infrastructure projects ADW Johnson is involved with, there will be an opportunity to work on diverse projects in a supportive and stimulating environment.
Successful candidates will undertake engineering studies at TAFE, typically one day a week, as part of a recognised traineeship. The remaining four days will be spent in the office where you will be provided on-the-job training and mentoring. In addition to a competitive salary, all TAFE fees for your studies will be reimbursed.
Reporting directly to the Drafting Coordinator some of your responsibilities will include:
·       Plan drafting and communicating with the supervisor in relation to job status; 
·       Liaising with your supervisor and other staff in relation to workload planning and drafting instructions;
·       Working effectively and collaboratively as part of a project team; and
·       Completing quality assurance checklists.
This role offers the following benefits:
·       An exciting opportunity to work with some of NSW's leading developers;
·       Variety of projects, including land development, high-end residential, and infrastructure, from planning through to construction completion;
·       Paid TAFE certification;
·       A tailored career development program for career advancement;
·       A steady stream of interesting projects;
·       A positive work environment with flexible hours and social activities;
·       Competitive salary based on skills and experience;
·       Access to a generous overtime system.
About You 
The ideal candidate will have recently completed their School Certificate or HSC, or begun a Drafting course at TAFE, with a keen interest in pursuing a drafting career. Desired skills include:
·       Excellent communication skills and the ability to work collaboratively in a team;
·       Enthusiasm and a passion for the construction and engineering industries;
·       Strong written and verbal communication abilities;
·       A strong work ethic and keen attention to detail.

What if you could do the kind of work the world needs?
At WSP, you can access our global scale, contribute to landmark projects and connect with the brightest minds in your field to do the best work of your life. You can embrace your curiosity in a culture that celebrates new ideas and diverse perspectives. You can experience a world of opportunity and the chance to shape a career as unique as you.
This role will see you enhance your capabilities and the reputation of WSP’s Building Structures team. You will collaborate with talented professionals working on iconic projects to drive future ready outcomes that will benefit clients and communities.
Our WSP Building Structures group are a specialist team renowned for their innovation in structural engineering and cutting-edge BIM project execution across high-rise and complex building structures and infrastructure projects, with offices in every major city across Australia.
We operate as a highly autonomous and genuinely national team. The ability to grow and develop your career at WSP are unparalleled in the market. We offer the opportunity to contribute to local and national buildings projects, plus the ability to expand your design skills across other market sectors.
Our recent projects span across a range of different sectors including but not limited to high-rise developments, schools, infrastructure, the list goes on. Some of our recent projects include:
- City Tattersalls Club Redevelopment
 - Sydney Fish Market
 - Sydney Harbourside
 - Shellharbour Hospital
 - 2 Chifley Square
At WSP you’ll find the scale and reach you need to do the kind of work the world needs – and the culture and people that make it the best work of your life.
What you’ll do:
- Project lead work across the design, delivery and tender phases for multi-year/packaged work for turnkey projects;
 - Ensure timely and quality of delivery for project and structural engineering work in support of relevant technical, commercial and regulatory standards – and in alignment with schedules and budgets;
 - Provide practical engineering advice and recommendations relating to site compliance and construction outcomes;
 - Handle ongoing communication and highly effective professional relationships with local clients;
 - Manage effective stakeholder relationships, both internally and externally;
 - Mentor, train and develop the careers of junior engineers;
 - Partner with internal stakeholders and a collaborative, national team in a multidisciplinary engineering setting;
Skills & Required Experience
- Bachelor to Masters’ level degree in Civil/Structural Engineering;
 - 4-10 years industry experience in Australia on building projects in the commercial, retail, defence, health or education sectors;
 - Solid proficiency in all-round structural engineering design including post-tensioned concrete;
 - Track record of effective cross-discipline project delivery; 
 - Strong communication skills and the ability to engage confidently with site personnel and clients;
 - The ability to lead, train and mentor junior engineers across technical and project delivery aspects;
 - Naturally Curious, Passionate, Adaptable & ready to do the kind of work the world needs;
Imagine a better future for you and a better future for us all.
Join our close-knit community of talented individuals who share your passion for making a positive impact. Our global team includes more than 80,000 employees, working together to make a difference in communities both close to home and around the world.
An employee Share Purchase Plan is available to all our permanent employees who wish to become owners and vested partners in WSP’s collective success. To find out more about our commitment to the health and wellbeing of our people, and the programs we’ve designed to help you thrive, go to our Employee Benefits page.
- Develop your professional network (locally, nationally and globally) through various initiatives.
 - Develop your personal brand through targeted training.
 - Develop your business understanding and awareness through various procedures.
WSP prioritises the health and wellbeing of our people by offering flexible working, 12 months parental leave, opportunities for global mobility, purchased additional leave, and competitive remuneration among many more benefits designed to help you shine.
We are committed to providing an inclusive, diverse and equal opportunity workplace. We promote Indigenous voices and are actively delivering a ‘Stretch’ level Reconciliation Action Plan. Accredited by the Workplace Gender Equality Agency as an Employer of Choice, we also support the LGBTQI+ community, and encourage all employees to bring their whole selves to work.
With us, you can. Apply today.
Recruitment agencies: our Talent Acquisition team recruits directly and will contact selected partners if external support is required.
